{:db/id 17592186162082 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186161895 :question/id #uuid "fdab3229-66ca-59d3-ac20-8a5b3d3506fc" :question/math-academy-id "e-9471" :question/problem "![](images/84/84de7754ed9244e3d646e452f6ed6dab349c130d17eae1d4dbc94cb52bd761e1.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above, traversed once counterclockwise." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/f4/f4e80a23910612bd55e7578a074f23c76535139889faff479c4dd0521e7496ff.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C = C_1 \\cup C_2 \\cup C_3$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s =  \\int_{C_1}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_2}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s + \\int_{C_3}f(x,y)\\,\\textrm d s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = L.\n$$\n\nThe path $C_1$ is a semicircle of radius $r = 3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_1} \\,\\textrm ds = \\dfrac{1}{2}(2 \\pi r) = 3\\pi.\n$$\n\nThe paths $C_2$ and $C_3$ are hypotenuses of right triangles whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\int_{C_2} \\,\\textrm ds = \\int_{C_3} \\,\\textrm ds = \\sqrt{3^2 + 4^2} = 5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\,\\textrm d s = 3\\pi + 5 + 5 = 3\\pi + 10.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e60b3dd1-0842-562d-a72f-5adb6a60cba8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050975 :topic/math-academy-id 459 :topic/title "The Distance Formula"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186162327 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac6987e-1443-5102-be6c-7c404cb81a29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +1)" :db/id 17592186253751} {:answer/id #uuid "4848d525-4fed-5241-aa55-e8be28361018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi +2)" :db/id 17592186254286} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb762e8-b607-526d-970c-769c2e97b12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2)" :db/id 17592186254526} {:answer/id #uuid "a1ab8300-d36e-5b2f-b815-bf8f3c00e075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2\\pi +1)" :db/id 17592186255094} {:answer/id #uuid "f438f0f4-4512-5533-b108-0d1c4c07ad3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(\\pi +1)" :db/id 17592186255807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5fb762e8-b607-526d-970c-769c2e97b12a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2)" :db/id 17592186254526} :answer-field/id #uuid "02208297-3b6c-56a2-86c8-c39f569c53b4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186255921}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef2f2e1e-2df6-5eea-a523-f7500a9f7301" :question/math-academy-id "q-122481" :question/problem "![](images/55/558dbbc424725ca0d9bad628968489cc2e32d67136102290666ff055a634bc16.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is a path that traverses a semicircle of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/82/82fedadbb33b1747832bac25d9cda8e0b6b18b0fab411a870e90bc09ce47226e.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a semi-circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\pi r=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4=2(\\pi +2).\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186162328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "976609f5-9b7b-5cf5-8af9-7eda58f599e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2} + \\sqrt{3}" :db/id 17592186159171} {:answer/id #uuid "f5827111-0006-5c1b-ba8a-12b199fc5f54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π + 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186159172} {:answer/id #uuid "1e127cda-f337-5d92-a559-58f2b9959529" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "π + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186159173} {:answer/id #uuid "3f7e980f-41b3-58a9-b313-eb4e1299df8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{π}{2} + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186159174} {:answer/id #uuid "68d2396c-897e-51b5-9821-0211bcf63840" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2π + 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186159175}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9788a76e-e0cc-5a5d-b125-0a5dce44952b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186159170}] :question/id #uuid "e7cfc0f1-43a0-55ae-a985-5e79d8a25ecd" :question/math-academy-id "q-122484" :question/problem "![](images/52/5277642b981910a5da1dd00a1b9aa4db28c7db7fcacf33faf209eea3ec1e93ab.png)\n\nCalculate $\\displaystyle \\int_{C}ds$, where $C$ is a path that traverses a circular segment of radius $2$ once in the counterclockwise direction, as shown above."} {:db/id 17592186256725 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "461a27ae-9bae-56e4-a290-8a9b99dd2f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id 17592186254262} {:answer/id #uuid "48f7a64a-5065-5b48-9afa-0c3ec86372c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id 17592186254296} {:answer/id #uuid "7fa5f20e-2e73-5f1c-9c2f-9b1fb94075b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id 17592186254799} {:answer/id #uuid "8b6906ae-426e-569c-adc9-44144d8e41a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id 17592186254901} {:answer/id #uuid "a3313bd1-e6b1-51a4-ba38-134097b446aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186255109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fa5f20e-2e73-5f1c-9c2f-9b1fb94075b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id 17592186254799} :answer-field/id #uuid "37cd5012-6b1d-57b4-a60a-c7978b2ab3f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186256019}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "23524215-604c-5fbd-8acf-4af9e94c29ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-122828" :question/problem "![](images/39/39a7cb0b31cb5d906803063597ae968be8fba90f048a4d9745225de7c3f8d6db.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of three parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/05/058c7b33112329df321e61660df4f2d388f42ca40c0aae5b73a089a0251726e2.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}\\cup {C}_{3}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{3}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe paths ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{3}$ are line segments of length $3.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{3}}\\,\\text{d}s=3.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3+5+3=11.\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186256730 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48070546-d80f-5246-86a4-aa8d7aa99c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\pi +1" :db/id 17592186254279} {:answer/id #uuid "72a7d010-8a49-501c-a8b0-6c4408fdf75f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +2" :db/id 17592186254685} {:answer/id #uuid "96002547-d724-56a8-8e09-188ad7369cdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +4" :db/id 17592186254992} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1a64fc-def5-5882-88a7-756a23766b42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +3" :db/id 17592186255336} {:answer/id #uuid "c24b4875-c3c0-55e6-b7fe-e4f60d7affdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi +2" :db/id 17592186255405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "72a7d010-8a49-501c-a8b0-6c4408fdf75f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\pi +2" :db/id 17592186254685} :answer-field/id #uuid "01fb92ac-5f7f-5736-aab9-a7276e24a517" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186255920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f87f9aea-995d-5fa2-9903-84aef89b9be9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122843" :question/problem "![](images/d7/d7844777c0bb540ba337756f45c4d71a8a8e9f9c84372e01542892801efecce3.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/98/98f444851e2df505d4242d1f8e4be0d76f78babd5d9633d9ab0ec84c245fe364.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is three-quarters of a circle of radius $r=2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{3}{4}(2\\pi r)=3\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is a line segment of length $2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=3\\pi +2.\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186256731 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2461d307-3086-5a5c-b497-aa48ad65c133" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id 17592186253997} {:answer/id #uuid "2dbd98bc-e62d-5a92-bfa0-9c4e1787b547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2+\\sqrt{5})" :db/id 17592186254082} {:answer/id #uuid "65e5a51e-ba13-5ae9-a263-385c9c9cf5de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(3+\\sqrt{5})" :db/id 17592186254582} {:answer/id #uuid "a1016a1d-d5a6-5066-9d4a-cb08a1cf0136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id 17592186255084} {:answer/id #uuid "b2237b88-2d33-5dfc-a776-cc65d79f2e63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id 17592186255236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a1016a1d-d5a6-5066-9d4a-cb08a1cf0136" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5+2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id 17592186255084} :answer-field/id #uuid "a64d136c-2e50-5fe9-8693-5b8666a0d0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186256225}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "efd8621e-7cbb-5240-b849-bfa0535c815e" :question/math-academy-id "q-122845" :question/problem "![](images/68/68b3f78c29c9d7776efc2a78672ae53fe2e806d7ca6c3d663de8a16c03342132.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/27/27c19b56a24315f1105539afc441a33957dddf606b3410b86121e7cb8ed16973.png)\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $3$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=5.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle whose legs have lengths $2$ and $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=5+2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186256733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fbccd3-1730-54fc-9475-ad997c5afc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id 17592186253721} {:answer/id #uuid "21e53e95-7ec4-5c95-b9e3-453c9a2ed4f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2\\pi +\\sqrt{2})" :db/id 17592186253974} {:answer/id #uuid "44332bd0-327e-53e0-9733-797aa948733d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}}{4}" :db/id 17592186254249} {:answer/id #uuid "6169a709-a992-502e-9cbc-f73991286538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\pi +3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id 17592186254543} {:answer/id #uuid "819bf68a-c423-5c96-b729-706e6eb1fc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id 17592186254817}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "819bf68a-c423-5c96-b729-706e6eb1fc6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id 17592186254817} :answer-field/id #uuid "4639a58d-2fdb-5f66-8101-7eaad8afbbd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186256053}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "65d60feb-29ba-53eb-9de0-464deb1c4c60" :question/math-academy-id "q-122850" :question/problem "![](images/bf/bf87c4707c0f4a8ab1b5157a13e8c7785da915833c5f9d896a2747af27f70e59.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above." :question/worked-solution "The path $C$ is made up of two parts, as shown below:\n\n![](images/ff/ff52b8e83a9cc9867b25ea3c24ed0f988a27dec73f9e0ab2dfda28ddabb3238a.png)\n\nCalculate ${\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s,$ where $C$ is the path shown above.\n\nNow, we make use of the following facts:\n\n- If $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}$ is a piecewise-smooth curve, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s+{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- The line integral of unity with respect to arc length over $C$ is equal to the arc length $L$ of $C,$ i.e.,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=L.\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ is a quarter of a circle of radius $r=4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{1}{4}(2\\pi r)=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe path ${C}_{2}$ is the hypotenuse of a right triangle where both legs have a length of $4.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}\\,\\text{d}s=\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}}=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}\\,\\text{d}s=2\\pi +4\\sqrt{2}=2(\\pi +2\\sqrt{2}).\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Line Integrals Over Piecewise-Smooth Curves"}
